  "method": "v1 (late-block attention rollout picks, cached teacher-map coverage as KD weight) with graded per-image token counts from the cached teacher map's effective token count (batch thirds 2/3, 1, 4/3 of K)",
  "paper": "Abnar & Zuidema ACL 2020 (attention rollout); Son et al. ECCV 2024 (MaskedKD); human TrustMask note 2026-10-28 ('how many?')",
  "why": "an image whose teacher evidence is concentrated keeps it with fewer tokens; a spread one loses it at a fixed K, so moving tokens from concentrated to spread images should keep the masked teacher's target closer to the full teacher at the same mean cost",
  "vs_maskedkd": "late-block rollout instead of last-block CLS attention, a per-image KD weight and per-image token counts from the cached teacher map (same mean teacher cost)",
  "prior_art": "Dynamic KD / DynKD allocate the teacher per sample all-or-nothing by student uncertainty; v2 grades token counts (no image without teacher) by the teacher's own attribution spread",
